    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bc5d425c0a67446f811292d08f896527",
      "statement": "DirectoryService construction binds a Store, the directory signing keypair, a DirectoryConfig and an injected Clock; it derives directory_fingerprint from the directory key, wires L2 DomainService eagerly and attaches L3 VouchService, L4 ReputationService, L4 ModerationService (receiving the reputation service) and L5 AuditService in _attach_subservices via lazy imports to avoid import cycles, then prunes expired entries on startup via store.prune_expired.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L39-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b45d1920c011df70147292fd1eafdb007cf8b52d1501ee22f7aee5bda64f77e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a59a9aa9f4c74367a0dc83792512947c",
      "statement": "Registration step 1 (submit_registration) validates the manifest and its canonical-JSON size cap, never trusts the client-supplied fingerprint but recomputes it from the presented public key (FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH), verifies the manifest signature, enforces capacity (an already-live fingerprint may re-register; otherwise DIRECTORY_FULL when count_live >= max_agents), and stores a single-use short-TTL challenge (nonce prefix v1:register:) bound to the key, endpoint and validated manifest snapshot with an audited insert_challenge.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L80-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e0bead2dbb2382a000d2304c253d0b3d5290c4f26893f2368b3533e57a571fa1:"
