    {
      "id": "claim_75cfe1ed20ae4111a84400b6d526dc97",
      "statement": "Registration step 2 (complete_registration) selects the challenge by challenge_id or, for legacy clients without one, the latest pending endpoint challenge for the fingerprint; it then checks fingerprint match, single-use (CHALLENGE_USED), expiry against the injected clock (CHALLENGE_EXPIRED), optional key binding (KEY_MISMATCH) and verifies the endpoint proof as an Ed25519 signature by the bound key over the challenge nonce (PROOF_INVALID).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L134-L185",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c122cc25cd0641d7d2755ece75825aa3bb0f0782506468ecd2bd2635ee7a08f7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_27eefaf64a9b47b38bff376bf6628531",
      "statement": "Store.complete_registration atomically consumes the challenge and lists the agent: inside one write transaction it re-checks the used flag under the write lock so a replayed completion loses the race with CHALLENGE_USED, marks the challenge used, upserts the agent row with a fresh TTL, and appends register.completed (fresh listing) or register.updated (re-registration of a still-live entry); live re-registration preserves registered_at/registered_epoch so trust-block age survives, while an expired or absent fingerprint starts a fresh listing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/store.py#L389-L446",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba06dbfaa62c07f29d992ba101e5ddd211b1489f21d20e246718fb32279ba7c8:"
