    {
      "id": "claim_0309122b23e5407b84c69faf80ee54de",
      "statement": "L2 DomainService proves domain control server-side: request_verification requires a live listing, a signature over the body subset (fingerprint, domain, method), a validated bare domain and method in {dns_txt, https_well_known}, then mints a 30-minute single-use token (config.domain_token_ttl_s); confirm re-verifies the signature and challenge state, requires the listing endpoint host to be the domain or a subdomain of it (DOMAIN_ENDPOINT_MISMATCH), delegates the actual DNS/TLS control check to the injected Resolver seam (stable codes DNS_TXT_NOT_FOUND, WELL_KNOWN_NOT_FOUND, WELL_KNOWN_MISMATCH, DNS_ERROR_TEMPORARY), and persists a config.domain_verification_ttl_days (90-day) verification atomically with audit domain.verified. primary_verification returns the most recently verified active record whose domain the endpoint host lives under for the trust block.",
      "evidence": [
