    {
      "id": "claim_ac417b5f43944e95b1d0ab74e56f4366",
      "statement": "L4 ReputationService runs transparent automata over signed reports: create_report validates category/severity/evidence-kind against closed sets, requires a live target and a live reporter whose listing tenure of at least config.report_tenure_hours (72 h) sets the counts eligibility flag, verifies the reporter signature, and dedupes (reporter, target, category) within the dup window. When a counting report in an abuse class (spam, phishing, impersonation_attempt, endpoint_hijack) is recorded, _maybe_auto_suspend suspends the target iff at least config.auto_suspend_threshold (3) unique eligible reporters exist in the report_window_days (7-day) window, writing through store.suspend_agent with actor directory and event report.auto_suspend. Signal reads stay raw: counters use the report_decay_days (180-day) window, and block_recommendation is a pure function returning a rate suggestion only when at least 2 unique eligible reporters allege fraud or payment_fraud in the window — data, never enforcement.",
      "evidence": [
